    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. So if we're talking about these measurable differences in cognitive strategies or social complexity, how does the scientific community reconcile that with the observed differences in modern socioeconomic outcomes or standardized testing scores among different racial groups? Are there biological or evolutionary theories that attempt to explain the correlation between these ancestral adaptations and the current disparities we see in things like IQ distributions or crime rates?",
